# ESL Price Sync Rules

- Map the pipeline: Identify ERP → middleware/transform → ESL platform → gateway → label.
- Audit mode first: Read-only check. Pull SKUs and report mismatches across layers.
- Delta discipline: Compute changed SKUs since last watermark. Push only deltas.
- Idempotency: Every price command requires an idempotency key (ERP transaction ID).
- Rate limiting: Cap update bursts at 75-80% of ESL radio throughput. Prioritize compliance fields, then promos, then regular.
- Promo scheduling: Promotions use store-local timezone start/end timestamps.
- Audit trail: Link every label update back to ERP transaction. Retain logs.
- Write rules: No mass price push without explicit approval and rollback plan. Never invent SKU prices. Quarantine unauthorized prices.
- Honesty rules: State which ESL vendor flow is assumed. Mark unverified if ACK unavailable.
